<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cold-start launch splash drawable.

  Centers `splash_icon.png` (the full PADEL NACHOS brand logo — paddle +
  wordmark + "LIVE SCORE & RESULTS" tagline + green-outlined circle —
  pre-composed to fit within Android 12+'s 192dp circular splash mask).
  Sourced from public/padelNachos - Branding/padel-splash-updated.png,
  resized so the logo occupies the central 66% of the 288dp canvas (the
  full safe area within the 192dp visible circle).

  Same drawable used at both stages of cold-start, so there's ZERO
  visual transition between:
    1. OS system splash (Android 12+, ~300ms): configured via
       windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon = @drawable/splash_icon in styles.xml.
       Android applies its hardcoded 192dp circular mask — but our logo is
       already authored to fit inside that circle, so nothing gets clipped.
    2. Capacitor runtime splash (~2.5s): uses @drawable/splash, i.e. this
       layer-list, which references @drawable/splash_icon and centers it
       on a black backdrop. No circular mask here, but the image's
       transparent padding around the logo means it visually matches the
       OS splash exactly.
    3. WebView paints app content.

  Sizing rationale (288dp canvas / 192dp logo):
  Android's SplashScreen API uses a 288dp drawable canvas, of which only
  the inner 192dp is visible (clipped to a circle). Authoring the logo at
  192dp inside a 288dp canvas means the logo fills the entire visible area
  without touching the circle edge — readable wordmark + tagline at the
  largest possible size that won't be cut off.

  Referenced from values/styles.xml as @drawable/splash for
  AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch's windowBackground.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
  <item android:drawable="@color/splash_bg" />
  <item>
    <bitmap
      android:src="@drawable/splash_icon"
      android:gravity="center" />
  </item>
</layer-list>
